\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How to Use Font Effectively
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Paragraph and Letter Spacing
\f1\b0 : Ensure adequate spacing between paragraphs and proper kerning (spacing between letters). This enhances readability and prevents text from appearing cluttered or overly dense.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Capital and Lowercase Letters
\f1\b0 : Use fonts that have clear differences in height between capital and lowercase letters. This distinction helps in distinguishing between different letters and improves overall text clarity.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Character Shape Distinction
\f1\b0 : Avoid fonts where characters like 'o', 'e', 'a', and 'c' look too similar to each other. Clear differentiation between these shapes is crucial to prevent misreading and enhance readability.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Font Weight and Width
\f1\b0 : Steer clear of fonts that are too thin or narrow. Such fonts can be hard to read, especially in smaller sizes or for people with visual impairments. Opt for medium to bold weights for better visibility.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Color Compliance
\f1\b0 : Ensure that font color contrasts well with the background. High contrast improves readability and makes text more accessible, especially for individuals with color vision deficiencies. Follow WCAG guidelines for color contrast to ensure accessibility.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 Balancing Act in Design
\f1\b0 : Every design process is a balancing act between these different challenges. It's essential to find the right mix of spacing, character distinction, weight, and color contrast to create an effective and accessible design. Balancing these elements thoughtfully will result in a more readable and visually appealing outcome.}